I generally take the large number of skills options as a DevTeam
trap.  Get new folks to overspend on skill slots early on that end
up making the late game harder.

So as I play a class how I approach skill slots evolved game to
game and year to year.  Early on I enhanced without much
planning.  Then I learned to plan my enhancements per class.
If I need to enhance some weapon to be able to survive a level
then I do that but I have a general plan of what spell schools and
weapons classes I will eventually want based on artifact
expectations.

